	using h for .y'y since it's easier to see as syllable initial.
Which =20

	seems to be the opposite of what you're saying.

	{ti'u} counts, as far as I know, all as one syllable since y'y
is not =20

	a syllable break. If it were, then cmavo like {ba'o} would be
